<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Q1 current account deficit 20 mln punts-CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish Q1 current account deficit 20 mln punts-CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's current account deficit was a preliminary 20 million punts in the first quarter of 1996, Central Statistics Office figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The current account deficit in the first quarter a year ago was 82 million punts, and the overall current account for 1995 showed a surplus of 918 million punts.</p>
<p>				  1996 Q1  1995 Q1   1995 year</p>
<p>    Current account	-20	-82	  918</p>
<p>    Merchandise	     1926     1483	7277</p>
<p>    Invisibles	     -1946    -1565     -6359</p>
<p>				(figures in millions of punts)</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
